   "unmapped": [
    "At each step the learner pulls a single base arm (observing its reward) rather than a super arm; goal is to identify the optimal super arm (combinatorial pure exploration)",
    "Learner uses |I| (size of the super arm set), or 2^m as an upper bound"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "The arms $i\\in [m]$ are called base arms, and there is also a super arm set $\\mathcal{I} \\subseteq 2^{[m]}$. For each super arm $S \\in \\mathcal{I}$, its expected reward is $\\sum_{i\\in S} \\mu_i$. ... At each time step $t$, the learning policy $\\pi$ can either pull a base arm $i(t) \\in [m]$, or output a super arm $S(t) \\in \\mathcal{I}$. The goal of the learning policy is to make sure that with probability at least $1-\\delta$, its output $S(t) = S^*$."
  },
